      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT to understand what needs to be improved.Now I'll check the working directory for the compile setup and scaffolding.Now I'll write the improved test with better understandability — descriptive method name, clearer intent, and removing cryptic/empty comments.The improved test compiles successfully. The changes made for better understandability: replaced the cryptic `// Undeclared exception!` comment and empty catch-block comments with a Javadoc explaining that valid values are 1–366 and that a negative input must throw `DateTimeException`, and removed unused imports — all while keeping the exact same method call (`DayOfYear.of(-408)`), exception type, and assertions."
